WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.961
Be sure to turn on
your electronic devices

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:06.172 position:61%
in order to fully enjoy the experience.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:10.927 line:0%
The story of <i>Tales of the City</i>
is one of quiet revolution.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:11.886
Whatcha doin'?

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.473 position:58%
Feeling the vibes of fiery resistance
seeping into my skin.

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.809 line:0%
We find we're able to still
push the conversation forward,

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:20.562 position:61%
<i>extending it to the younger generation.</i>

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.063 position:59%
And it's the opportunity of a lifetime

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:26.359 position:63%
to come back to something that was truly
a formative experience for me.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:30.155 position:61% line:0%
People have been talking about bringing
<i>Tales</i> back over the past 25 years.

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:32.407
<i>But the reason for it being redone</i>

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.827
<i>had to be in response
to the world we're living in now.</i>

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.497 position:66%
A couple of queers walk down the street
and no one knows it. Are they still queer?

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:42.876
Barbary Lane is a magical place

00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:46.212
<i>that exists a little outside
the real world.</i>

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:50.049
You'll find I'm not particularly
literal about these things.

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:54.262
Literal's for the unimaginative.

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:55.889
Action!

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:00.143 position:56%
<i>Just as Barbary Lane is a safe place
for our characters,</i>

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.604 position:56%
I wanted the show to be a safe space
for viewers.

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:07.233 position:66%
Inherently, within towns, there is a sense
of family and a sense of home.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.402
It's got a little community.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.031 line:0%
These friendships and relationships

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:16.659 position:61%
<i>are all about letting you be the person
who you wanna be.</i>

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.828
What's up, millennial?

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.164
Do not ever call me that again.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.792 position:59% line:0%
Generations that seem light years away

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:27.128 line:0%
actually can reach common ground
and understand each other.

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:28.838
<i>It's just a matter of listening.</i>

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.674 position:61%
So, it's time to regroup and show again

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.219
<i>how a loving community
can become a family.</i>

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:35.762
What do you think is up there?

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.263
Rich white people.

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:44.145 position:63%
A lot of the season is structured around
Anna Madrigal and a flashback to 1966.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.105
<i>A secret that she has.</i>

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.109 position:56%
Comptons was basically
the Rosa Parks bus of trans history.

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.861
Girls, this is Anna.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.947
<i>We see Anna's experience</i>

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.950 position:56%
juxtaposed against these trans women
that she falls into.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.410
<i>Those men, the ones you drink 
and dance with,</i>

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:02.413 position:56%
those men are killing us one by one.

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:05.291
<i>Predominantly, marginalized people,
in some ways,</i>

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.752
potentially being rejected
from their family,

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:10.296 position:63%
<i>you know, have to form their own family.</i>

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.175
This feels too good to be true.

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:16.594
My mother used to say,

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.429
-"There's only the truth."
-There's only the truth.

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:21.224 line:0%
In any community,
race, culture, class, all of it,

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.602 position:58% line:0%
it shows that we can all be different
and still experience the same things.

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:26.229
A new generation.

00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:32.443
<i>Isn't it beautiful
and also terribly depressing?</i>

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:33.695
<i>Terribly.</i>

00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:38.366 line:0%
The books and the series
are such cult classics.

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:40.493
This is surreal.

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:42.829
I produced the original in 1994.

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:45.957
<i>We were making a love letter
to San Francisco</i>

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:52.589 position:66%
and a love letter to a new, all-embracing,
nonjudgmental version of family.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:58.177 position:66% line:0%
For the viewer,
I think, it just widens their perspective.

00:02:58.261 --> 00:03:00.972
<i>I think it's especially good
for younger people</i>

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:04.475 position:63%
<i>and makes their humanity more inclusive.</i>

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:06.644
You don't wish for what's to come.

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:10.523
You revel in what's already here.

